    "headingPashto": "الویولونه",
    "urduTitle": "ہوائی تھیلے",
    "text": "The alveoli form the gas exchange surface. The wall of each alveolus is only 0.1 μm thick. On its outsides is a dense network of blood capillaries. Lining each alveolus is moist squamous epithelium.\n\ntidbit\nThere are over 700 million alveoli present in the lungs, representing a total surface area of 70-90m.\n\nThis consists of very thin, flattened cells, reducing the distance over which diffusion must occur. Collagen and elastic fibres are also present which allow the alveoli to expand and recoil easily during breathing.",
