     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">Their long loops of Henle extend deep into the medulla.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">The loops contribute to the medullary osmotic gradient through countercurrent processes.</li><li data-example-step=\"2\" style=\"display:none;\">This gradient supports water reabsorption and concentrated urine when water is scarce.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>Their long loops create and use a deep medullary gradient that enables effective water conservation.</div>",
