     "qNo": "vi",
     "q": "How ADH controls concentration of urine?",
     "steps": [
      "Water shortage stimulates ADH release from the posterior pituitary.",
      "ADH increases the water permeability of collecting ducts and the relevant distal nephron regions.",
      "More water returns to the blood, so urine volume falls and concentration rises.",
      "When ADH release is low, less water is reabsorbed and more dilute urine is produced."
     ],
     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">Water shortage stimulates ADH release from the posterior pituitary.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">ADH increases the water permeability of collecting ducts and the relevant distal nephron regions.</li><li data-example-step=\"2\" style=\"display:none;\">More water returns to the blood, so urine volume falls and concentration rises.</li><li data-example-step=\"3\" style=\"display:none;\">When ADH release is low, less water is reabsorbed and more dilute urine is produced.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>More ADH produces less, more concentrated urine; less ADH produces more dilute urine.</div>",
