     "desc": "<p>Describe the importance of kidney donation for the benefit of kidney failure patients.</p><p><strong>SpaceBook learning answer:</strong> A suitable donated kidney can restore filtration and other kidney functions in a patient with end-stage kidney failure and may free the recipient from dialysis. Donor–recipient compatibility, transplantation care and control of rejection are important. Donation connects biological knowledge with an opportunity to improve another person’s health and daily life.</p>",
