     "qNo": "iii",
     "q": "What are types of fractures? Describe the repair process of a simple fracture.",
     "steps": [
      "A simple or closed fracture leaves the skin intact; an open or compound fracture communicates with a skin wound.",
      "Hematoma formation: torn vessels bleed and a clot forms at the break.",
      "Fibrocartilaginous callus formation: new vessels and repair cells enter; a soft callus bridges the broken ends.",
      "Bony callus formation: the soft callus is replaced by a harder bridge of spongy bone.",
      "Remodeling: bone is reorganized in response to mechanical stresses, restoring its structure."
     ],
     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">A simple or closed fracture leaves the skin intact; an open or compound fracture communicates with a skin wound.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">Hematoma formation: torn vessels bleed and a clot forms at the break.</li><li data-example-step=\"2\" style=\"display:none;\">Fibrocartilaginous callus formation: new vessels and repair cells enter; a soft callus bridges the broken ends.</li><li data-example-step=\"3\" style=\"display:none;\">Bony callus formation: the soft callus is replaced by a harder bridge of spongy bone.</li><li data-example-step=\"4\" style=\"display:none;\">Remodeling: bone is reorganized in response to mechanical stresses, restoring its structure.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>The two source fracture types are closed and open; repair proceeds through hematoma, soft callus, bony callus and remodeling.</div>",
