     "qNo": "v",
     "q": "Explain the ultra-structure of human skeletal muscles.",
     "steps": [
      "A skeletal muscle contains bundles of long muscle fibres. Each fibre has a sarcolemma surrounding sarcoplasm with peripheral nuclei, mitochondria, glycogen and myoglobin.",
      "T tubules carry excitation inward, while the sarcoplasmic reticulum stores and releases calcium.",
      "The fibre contains myofibrils composed of repeating sarcomeres between successive Z lines.",
      "Thin actin filaments and thick myosin filaments form the banding pattern; thin filaments also contain troponin and tropomyosin.",
      "The A band corresponds to the thick-filament length, the I band contains thin filaments without thick overlap, and the H zone is the central thick-only region. The M line lies centrally."
     ],
     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">A skeletal muscle contains bundles of long muscle fibres. Each fibre has a sarcolemma surrounding sarcoplasm with peripheral nuclei, mitochondria, glycogen and myoglobin.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">T tubules carry excitation inward, while the sarcoplasmic reticulum stores and releases calcium.</li><li data-example-step=\"2\" style=\"display:none;\">The fibre contains myofibrils composed of repeating sarcomeres between successive Z lines.</li><li data-example-step=\"3\" style=\"display:none;\">Thin actin filaments and thick myosin filaments form the banding pattern; thin filaments also contain troponin and tropomyosin.</li><li data-example-step=\"4\" style=\"display:none;\">The A band corresponds to the thick-filament length, the I band contains thin filaments without thick overlap, and the H zone is the central thick-only region. The M line lies centrally.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>Skeletal muscle is organized as muscle → bundles → fibres → myofibrils → sarcomeres → thick and thin filaments.</div>",
