     "title": "Compare the structure of skeleton, smooth and cardiac muscles with the help of prepared slides.",
     "desc": "<p><strong>SpaceBook learning answer:</strong> Record the actual slides: skeletal muscle has long parallel striated fibres and multiple peripheral nuclei; cardiac muscle has branching striated cells and intercalated discs; smooth muscle has spindle-shaped cells, a central nucleus and no striations. Do not invent features that are not visible at the available magnification.</p>",
