     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">Cranial bones: frontal, occipital, sphenoid and ethmoid are unpaired; parietal and temporal are paired. This gives eight cranial bones.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">Facial bones: mandible and vomer are unpaired; maxilla, zygomatic, lacrimal, nasal, inferior nasal concha and palatine are paired. This gives fourteen facial bones.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>Eight cranial bones form the cranium and fourteen facial bones form the face, as listed in Table16.3.</div>",
