     "q": "Describe the structure of bone.",
     "steps": [
      "Bone is living connective tissue containing cells embedded in a hard, mineralized matrix.",
      "Its organic component is chiefly collagen, which contributes flexibility and tensile strength. Inorganic calcium-phosphate-rich mineral gives hardness.",
      "Osteoblasts produce bone matrix; osteocytes are mature bone cells within it; osteoclasts resorb bone during remodeling.",
      "Bone has blood vessels that support its living cells and metabolic exchange.",
      "The chapter gives two approximate organic/inorganic ratios in different paragraphs; use the qualitative distinction between collagen and mineral rather than treating the two printed ratios as identical."
     ],
     "answer": "<div><strong>SpaceBook learning answer</strong><ol><li data-example-step=\"0\" style=\"\">Bone is living connective tissue containing cells embedded in a hard, mineralized matrix.</li><li data-example-step=\"1\" style=\"display:none;\">Its organic component is chiefly collagen, which contributes flexibility and tensile strength. Inorganic calcium-phosphate-rich mineral gives hardness.</li><li data-example-step=\"2\" style=\"display:none;\">Osteoblasts produce bone matrix; osteocytes are mature bone cells within it; osteoclasts resorb bone during remodeling.</li><li data-example-step=\"3\" style=\"display:none;\">Bone has blood vessels that support its living cells and metabolic exchange.</li><li data-example-step=\"4\" style=\"display:none;\">The chapter gives two approximate organic/inorganic ratios in different paragraphs; use the qualitative distinction between collagen and mineral rather than treating the two printed ratios as identical.</li></ol><button type=\"button\" data-revealed=\"1\" onclick=\"revealMathExampleStep(this)\">Next step</button> <button type=\"button\" onclick=\"resetMathExampleSteps(this)\">Start again</button></div><div data-example-answer style=\"display:none;margin-top:.7rem;\"><strong>Answer: </strong>Bone consists of living cells in a collagen-and-mineral matrix and is continually maintained and remodeled.</div><p>Reference: <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/6-3-bone-structure\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenStax — bone structure</a>.</p>",
     "plainAnswer": "Bone consists of living cells in a collagen-and-mineral matrix and is continually maintained and remodeled.",
     "solutionOrigin": "SpaceBook learning answer",
