    "editorialNotes": [
     "Fig 22.12 prints \"Fruit Files\" and \"White-eyed male(Sport)\"; both preserved.",
     "Fig 22.13 as printed lists the male's gametes as \"50% Xᴿ\" and \"50% Y\" and labels the 50% F₁ male \"XᴿXᴿ\", although its own Punnett square and caption give Xʷ and XᴿY. These printed label errors are reproduced, not silently corrected. The figure also prints \"1,237 red-eyed files\".",
     "Fig 22.14 caption prints \"white eyed flics\"; read as \"flies\" (scan blur).",
     "Fig 22.15 caption: \"Morgan wanted to test his hypothesis .he crossed F₁ females ... with white-eyed male\" — the figure header labels the male \"F₂ ♂ (XʷY)\". Punctuation and labels preserved.",
     "Fig 22.16 prints \"Redeyed female\" and \"White eyal male\"; preserved.",
     "The numbering goes from 22.8.1 to 22.8.3; there is no 22.8.2 heading in the source.",
     "Printed \"a daughter gets as X chromosome\" preserved.",
     "Printed \"reccssive\" and \"determined by as X – linked recessive gene\" preserved.",
     "Printed \"daughters posses their fathers' X-chromosome\" preserved.",
     "The father's genotypes are printed with superscripts (X with superscript c for the colour-blind allele, X with superscript C for the normal allele); they are written here as X^cY and X^CY.",
     "Fig 22.17 genotype superscripts are small in the scan; the colour-blind allele is shown as X^c, the normal allele as X^C and the uncertain female as X^C X^? following the printed explanatory note. The note prints \"Assigning genotypes to the mate\", \"The lalar are caulers of the of the\" (scan) — read from the image as \"male\" and \"The later are carriers of the of the\"; \"Son' children\" preserved.",
     "Printed p.223 carries only the baldness example; the rest of the page is blank in the source."
    ]
